From 5902333ab735bb12f2e3c08865c7a51694a5a58e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:57:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Library] Dolby Vision: the enhancement layer by the bridge's
 rule, and p3i's infolabels

Kodi 22 keeps the Dolby Vision profile of a file in the video library, in
the columns it already has: its HDR detail ("5", "7FEL", "7MEL", "8.1",
"8.4"; strHdrDetail) and, for a stream that carries HDR10+ too or a base
layer in HLG, a second, virtual, video stream of that HDR type. A library
shared over MySQL with other Kodi 22 systems keeps what each one writes, and
skins read it (ListItem.HdrDetail, ListItem.Property(HdrType.N) and
HdrDetail.N). So Hades keeps it there too, with no column and no store of
its own; what it adds:

- The enhancement layer of a profile 7 stream is judged by the rule that
  draws it (the bridge's, tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_mel.h, and libplacebo's
  pl_avdovi_nlq_is_trivial()): KODI::UTILS::DOLBYVISION::ElType() in
  utils/DolbyVisionLibrary.h, which DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg now sets in
  strDVELType. Kodi's took vdr_in_max 1 as 1 << 23 whatever the RPU's own
  denominator (coef_log2_denom), said nothing for a residual that the RPU
  disables (that is MEL), nor for a layer of the base layer's size.
- CDVDFileInfo reads, of a profile 7 stream, the RPU of each access unit
  that it reads to decode one picture, before anything is decoded, as the
  bridge reads it (dvbridge_residual_probe_*() in dvbridge_probe.c, over
  dvbridge_rpu_nlq_packet()), and while none can carry a residual a few
  more, not decoded: 48 access units of the stream at most, and 16 MiB of
  what the demuxer gives of all its streams. FEL
  where one of them, or the decoded picture, can carry a residual; MEL where
  every one read says no residual; otherwise what the picture says
  (StreamElType()). The library said FEL or MEL from one picture, a fifth
  into the file; a stream whose RPUs change within groups of pictures could
  be called MEL. A stream that does not decode still gets what its RPUs say.
- ListItem.DvProfile and ListItem.HdrTypeAlt, the infolabels of p3i's
  CoreELEC (pannal/xbmc #56) with its values ("5.0", "7.6 FEL", "7.6 MEL",
  "7.6 EL", "8.1", "8.4"; "hdr10plus", "hlg"), from what the library keeps,
  so that skins made for it show them (ProfileName()).
- Estuary's information of a video shows the profile with those names:
  "Dolby Vision P7.6 FEL / HDR10+".

kodi.log says, for each profile 7 stream that is scanned, what the
enhancement layer is and what the RPUs read and the picture said. Nothing
changes in the database's schema or in what is written to it but the
enhancement layer of profile 7 ("7FEL", "7MEL", as Kodi writes it).
